{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:62833b17108e3814","name":"Vagaari Infiltrator","source":{"id":"source:reference-62833b17108e3814","title":"Vagaari Infiltrator","revision":21477,"timestamp":"2024-08-26T01:52:11Z","sha256":"4f52f175dd21b98226aa9859317ff5c4078e7ec8a87860484957bb17d11ef54c","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=21477","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=Vagaari%20Infiltrator&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-62833b17108e3814","blocks":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Unknown Regions Campaign Guide"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Unknown_Regions_Campaign_Guide"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Affiliations: ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Vagaari Empire"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Vagaari_Empire","referenceId":"reference:15aa603212aaa0f7"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Before ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Vagaari Empire"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Vagaari_Empire","referenceId":"reference:15aa603212aaa0f7"}," launches an assault on another world, they first send out a small number of Vagaari Infiltrators- slavers disguised as traders and explorers- to make peaceful contact with the planets that are potential targets. Many civilizations in ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Unknown Regions"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Unknown_Regions"}," are eager to find trading partners, so these infiltrators often end up being welcomed in ways that are not extended to more official explorers (particularly those of military groups like ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Chiss Ascendancy"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Chiss_Ascendancy","referenceId":"reference:410c64a9afa98052"},"). These Vagaari Infiltrators ingratiate themselves with the locals, engage in limited trade, and build up goodwill, all the while collecting data about the planet's defenses and customs and about optimal target sites. Eventually, the Infiltrators depart, continuing along their supposed trade route. Within a matter of days, ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Vagaari Empire"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Vagaari_Empire","referenceId":"reference:15aa603212aaa0f7"}," slaver fleet arrives at that planet, taking advantage of the scouting done by the Vagaari Infiltrator.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Should a Vagaari Infiltrator's true plans be revealed, the Infiltrator relies on the element of surprise. Although strong and capable of defending themselves, most Vagaari Infiltrators are not soldiers and instead have cultivated their social skills and galactic knowledge. Vagaari Infiltrators forced into combat will use deceptive feints (made easier by the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Combat Trickery"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Combat_Trickery","referenceId":"reference:43885864d188aa20"}," feat) to expose their enemies to the bonus damage from their ",{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Sneak Attack"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Sneak_Attack"}]}," Talents. When it combines these feints with a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Stun Baton"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Stun_Baton","referenceId":"reference:895573ffa7826a58"}," or a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Blaster Pistol"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Blaster_Pistol","referenceId":"reference:38dcc06542ba096c"}," set on ",{"tag":"a","children":["Stun"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Stun"},", a Vagaari Infiltrator can quickly knock an enemy down the ",{"tag":"a","children":["Condition Track"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Condition_Track"}," in the hopes of making a hasty escape to a waiting ",{"tag":"a","children":["Space Transport"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Space_Transport"},".\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h2","children":["Vagaari Infiltrator Statistics (CL 5)"]},"\n",{"tag":"h4","children":["Normal"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["Medium ",{"tag":